{"id": "live-398", "title": "Deutsche Finance America LLC v. Bayerische Versorgungskammer (Delaware Contract and Defamation Suit Over $2B US CRE Portfolio)", "category": "reit-securities", "status": "pending", "date": "2026-09-01", "jurisdiction": "U.S. District Court for the District of Delaware (removed from Delaware Superior Court)", "state": null, "amount": "~$2B US property portfolio; BVK has flagged potential losses of up to €853M", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://www.bisnow.com/news/national/commercial-real-estate/deutsche-finance-alleges-bvk-responsible-cre-portfolio-losing-1b-dollars-new-lawsuit", "summary": "Deutsche Finance America LLC and its German parent sued Bayerische Versorgungskammer (BVK), Germany's largest public pension fund, in Delaware Superior Court on September 1, 2026, alleging breach of contract, defamation, and deceptive trade practices over a nearly $2 billion US commercial real estate portfolio. Deutsche Finance says BVK held sole authority over the portfolio's budgets, financing and leasing decisions, failed to act as the market weakened, and then falsely blamed Deutsche Finance for losses that could reach €853 million; BVK removed the case to federal court in October 2026 and rejects the allegations. Munich prosecutors searched both companies' offices on November 3 and 5, 2026 as part of a separate corruption probe into BVK's US real estate program.", "significance": "Shows how a governance dispute over who actually controlled a complex, cross-border real estate investment structure becomes the central battleground once a portfolio's losses need a party to blame, and how a civil contract fight of this size can draw in regulatory and criminal scrutiny of the parties' underlying business relationship. Institutional investors and asset managers structuring discretionary mandates or joint ventures for US commercial property should document decision-making authority in real time, since ambiguity on that point is exactly what each side is now litigating.", "judge": null, "tags": ["reit-securities", "pension-fund", "joint-venture", "delaware", "cross-border"]}
